        {
          "id": "the-taxpayer-executor-donor-or-an-authorized-representative-must-sign-if-your-last-return-was-a-joint-return-your-spouse-must-also-sign-unless-you-have-indicated-by-checking-the-box-on-line-1-that-you-are-establishing-a-separate-residence",
          "label": "The taxpayer, executor, donor, or an authorized representative must sign. If your last return was a joint return, your spouse must also sign (unless you have indicated by checking the box on line 1 that you are establishing a separate residence).",
          "response": "",
          "hints": {
            "expectedDataType": "boolean"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "if-you-are-a-representative-signing-on-behalf-of-the-taxpayer-you-must-attach-to-form-8822-a-copy-of-your-power-of-attorney-to-do-this-you-can-use-form-2848-the-internal-revenue-service-will-not-complete-an-address-change-from-an-unauthorized-third-party",
          "label": "If you are a representative signing on behalf of the taxpayer, you must attach to Form 8822 a copy of your power of attorney. To do this, you can use Form 2848. The Internal Revenue Service will not complete an address change from an 'unauthorized' third party.",
          "response": "",
          "hints": {
            "expectedDataType": "text"
